Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:12:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: route three channels to the Marble speaker TDM
 backend

Drive the top amplifier's ultrasound input in TDM slot 2 with the final FL/FR/FC channel layout.

Source changes (original messages and trailers follow).

Source-commit: 5ef79b849c66255ac0faa5adf16d157eaaf580d0
Source-author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Source-date: 2026-10-25T19:12:29+08:00
Imported-from: pkgs/linux-kernel/sm7475/marble/patches/local/0075-ASoC-qcom-audioreach-add-a-default-map-for-three-cha.patch

ASoC: qcom: audioreach: add a default map for three channels

audioreach_set_default_channel_mapping() fills maps for one, two and
four channels only. A three-channel backend keeps an empty map, and the
MFC output media format then carries no channel types.

Map three channels to front left, front right and front centre, the map
the Android audio HAL (PAL) uses for three-channel devices.

Re-applied after the LPASS DCODEC vote fix: the earlier attempt (reverted
by 81b63654fb5a/321f3d13156f/06be2e6db9f9) was tested while 7.3 sent no
audio to the amplifiers at all, so it could not show whether driving slot 2
removes the noise of the top amplifier (0x34), whose ACF takes TDM
ultrasound input (SYSCTRL ULS_MODE) and otherwise mixes an undriven slot.
Stock fills slot 2 from its ultrasound backend (TDM-LPAIF-RX-TERTIARY-VIRT-1,
silent when no ultrasound session runs); here the device MFC produces it as
the front-centre channel of its 2 -> 3 channel conversion, so the slot
carries a defined signal instead of an idle line.

(cherry picked from commit 3d6b32a6d7cf3ad1c4c1b92acf77d32d0a89e421)

